    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What is hibernation?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When it’s really cold and food is hard to find, some animals will fall into a deep “sleep”. They "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "curl up",
            "zh": "蜷缩"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in a safe place, and “sleep” through the winter. We call this “hibernation”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What animals are hibernators?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Animals that hibernate are called hibernators. Bats, snakes, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "hedgehogs",
            "zh": "刺猬"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", bears are good examples of hibernators. They like dark and quiet places. Some go "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "underground",
            "zh": "地下"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or into "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "caves",
            "zh": "山洞"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When winter is getting near, hibernators try to eat lots of food to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "store",
            "ref": "v-store"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " up "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "body fat",
            "zh": "脂肪"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Some collect food and store it. And at times, during hibernation, they "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "wake up",
            "ref": "v-wake-up"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to eat, and then go back to “sleep” again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sleeping or hibernating?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "During hibernation, the hibernator’s body "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "temperature",
            "ref": "v-temperature"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " drops. And its heart and breathing "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "rates",
            "zh": "呼吸频率"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " slow down. This doesn’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "happen",
            "ref": "v-happen"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " during sleep! Moreover, any noise will wake up a sleeping animal, but not a hibernator."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
